    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45280" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Statones</span></b> , um, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the people of Statonia
				in Southern Etruria</i>, <i>celebrated for its
				vines and stone-quarries</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				8, § 52</span></i>. —Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Statonĭensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Statonia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 95, 96</span></i>
			, 
			 § 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">209: vina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					14, 6, 8, § 67</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 3, 25, 8</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Statonĭensis</span></b> ,
				is, m. (sc. ager), <i><span class="en">Plin. 36,
				22, 49, § 168</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 3, 12</span></i>. 1.</div>
